WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.390
Two bottles carry the same
molecular formula: C₂H₆O.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.290
One holds a liquid that
boils at 78 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.170
The other holds a gas that boils at −24.

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.410
Same formula.

5
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.970
So how can C₂H₆O be both a liquid
and a gas at room temperature?

6
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.490
In this mission, you'll meet five
ways to write an organic formula,

7
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.130
and learn to read a skeletal one.

8
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.590
You'll learn to spot the functional
groups that decide a compound's class,

9
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.370
and tell look-alikes apart.

10
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:37.330
Your mission: explain how one formula
can be both a liquid and a gas.
